**Instance Purchasing options:

1. On demand Instances:
--> pay for what you use:
---> Linux and Windows = billing per second,after the first min.(70sec)--> 1 min 10 sec
---> all othet OS = billing per hour
--> has the highest cost but no upfront payment
--> no long term commitment
--> recommended for short term workload

2. Reserved Instance:
--> upto 72% discount compared to on demand
--> reservation period: 1 year or 3 years
--> payment options: No upfront, partial upfront, All upfront

3. Spot Instance:
--> can get a discount of up to 90% compared to on demand
--> spot instance --> ununsed instance capacity
--> the most cost efficient instance in AWS
--> used for testing, data analysis, or any distributed workload
--> not suitable for critical jobs or database

4. Dedicated host:
--> A physical server with 
ec2 instaance capacity fully dedicated to your use.
--> The most expensive option

5. Saving plans:
--> commit to a certain type of usage ($10/hour for 1 year or 3 years)

6. capacity reservation:
--> reserve on demand instances capacity in a specific AZ for any duration
--> you always have access to EC2 capacity when you need it.


